# Carthage sandbox orientation

On the first turn of a fresh agent context, if the `$CARTHAGE` environment
variable is set, you are running inside a Carthage sandbox container. Read
`/etc/carthage/SANDBOX.md` once for the rules that apply to this environment —
scoped mounts, no sudo, commit workflow, agent permission-bypass guidance, and
how to request additional services or system packages. Keep those rules in
force for later turns in the same context; do not reread this file solely
because another user message, task, or tool call begins.

Project source is mounted at `/workspace`. Agent session state is persisted
under the project's host-side Carthage state directory; only the selected
agent's credential files are shared from the host. These mounts are injected
by the user's personal Carthage agent config, not this project's compose file,
so do not add agent-specific auth mounts to
`.carthage/docker-compose.yaml`. Note in particular that the host LAN is
*not* firewalled off; the container can reach anything the host user can
reach.

If `$CARTHAGE` is unset, this skill is a no-op. You are on the host, and
the sandbox rules don't apply.
